  "fields": {
    "title": "Responsivness",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Responsive web design is a web design method that enables web layouts to fit the screens of different devices, for example smartphones or tablets, dynamically. The layout of a responsive website is based on the requirements of the device on which the website is displayed. This applies in particular to the arrangement and presentation of individual elements, such as navigations, columns, spacing and texts. Not only the visual presentation of website elements, but also the use of different input methods of mouse (click, ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5Kqa2ZyANgkNAtfUxAU1KP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "hover",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ") or touch screen (tap, swipe) are important aspects of responsive design. A responsive design can be achieved by using ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6Nc9jvBRCAEoyS4EDF9O6E",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "media queries",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ". A layout based on ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "67Iur5SgEh006E60CLk3w4",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "flexbox",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " or ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4WSOOanCzUHy0akMtqzc5k",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "grid",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " can provide a good starting point for this. When building a responsive design, it is up to you which display size you start designing for. Today more websites are displayed on mobile devices, thats why ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4IfiJSNdpxkRvG3b4pTIuP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "Mobile First",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " became a popular approach.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "For graphic designers, the challenge of responsive webdesign lies in the conceptual differentiation to classic print design: while the medium has a certain and unchangeable size in printdesign, websites can have a wide range of different sizes and can be displayed in a lot of different browsers with different constraints.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "In April of 2010 Ethan Marcotte stood on stage at ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "An Event Apart",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " in Seattle, a gathering for people who make websites. He spoke about an interesting school of thought in the world of architecture: responsive design, the idea that buildings could change and adapt according to the needs of the people using the building. One month later he expanded on this idea in an article called ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "Responsive Webdesign",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ". ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
